call_details.response:
The remaining empty positions admit only three possible winning lines under optimal play (all other 4-in-a-row windows on the board already contain both colors and are therefore permanently blocked):

- o completes the diagonal (0,0)-(1,1)-(2,2)-(3,3) by occupying (0,0);
- o completes the horizontal (0,3)-(0,4)-(0,5)-(0,6) by occupying all three of (0,4), (0,5) and (0,6);
- x completes the vertical (0,6)-(1,6)-(2,6)-(3,6) by occupying both remaining cells of column 6.

Playing column 4 immediately claims (0,4). Thereafter every reply by x opens at least one of the other two cells o needs (or the diagonal cell (0,0)). In each case o can answer by taking the newly threatened cell, completing a 4-in-a-row on the subsequent move. Consequently column 4 is a forced win.

Final Answer: 4

